{"id": "EUVD-2026-103454", "enisaUuid": "ccb3230c-9b11-3386-8ea6-2545e92fa001", "description": "ProjectSend 2.0.0 before 2.7.0 contains an incorrect authorization vulnerability that allows restricted API token holders to change the token owner's credentials via PATCH /api/v1/users/{user}. Attackers with a token limited to manage_users and edit_users can set a new owner password, clear two-factor authentication, and sign in interactively with the owner's full role permissions.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T11:38:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T15:55:45", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/projectsend/projectsend/security/advisories/GHSA-j5cp-r8pr-m5cr", "https://github.com/projectsend/projectsend/commit/db65731c3ad28ac7f0d541c60cb65eb100958514", "https://github.com/projectsend/projectsend/releases/tag/v2.7.0", "https://github.com/projectsend/projectsend/blob/v2.6.0/app/Modules/Identity/StaffAccounts.php#L153-L162", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/projectsend-2.0.0-before-2.7.0-incorrect-authorization-via-users-api-token-abilities"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7c3c-3r99-phc3", "CVE-2026-112001"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.49, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b29c881c-e087-3e39-9153-4ef00ef3f87e", "product": {"name": "ProjectSend", "vendor": {"name": "projectsend"}}, "product_version": "2.0.0 <2.7.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c61354be-8096-3813-b303-82badb782d6a", "vendor": {"name": "projectsend"}}], "isExploited": false}